
# ── HL7 / MLLP security (port 6661) ──────────────────────────────
# The MLLP listener has NO authentication: anyone who can reach port 6661 can
# inject HL7. Access is controlled by a source-IP whitelist applied to the
# DOCKER-USER iptables chain (published container ports bypass INPUT).
#
# HL7_ALLOWED_IPS: space- or comma-separated sender IPs/CIDRs. REQUIRED before
# running scripts/hl7_firewall.sh — the script refuses to run when empty rather
# than applying a deny-all that would take HL7 offline.
# Find the real senders:  docker compose logs rayd-app | grep -i mllp
#HL7_ALLOWED_IPS=10.20.30.40 10.20.30.41

# Optional defence in depth: bind the published port to one host interface.
# Leave unset (default 0.0.0.0) unless you know the correct NIC address.
# Do NOT set 127.0.0.1 — the PACS/HIS senders are remote and would be blocked.
#HL7_BIND_ADDR=0.0.0.0
